  "notes": "Issue #514. EXP-374 model, folds, seed, checkpoint policy, stop notation parser, Ensembl residue-position mask, canonical pathway-20 burden and pathway mutation-type composition are all held fixed and unchanged. The sole change adds four new sample-level burden columns (mutated_gene_count, lof_gene_count for each of two fixed lineage gene groups) from a new, independently literature-curated knowledge/kirc_kidney_glioma_lineage_v1.json panel: a kidney/VHL-mTOR lineage group (VHL, MTOR, TSC1, TSC2, PTEN, MET, FH) and a glioma/WHO-IDH lineage group (IDH1, IDH2, ATRX, TP53, NF1, PTEN, EGFR). Hypothesis: EXP-374 OOF error analysis found the two largest confusion pairs are KIPAN<->KIRC (390 combined misclassifications) and GBMLGG<->LGG (288 combined); these lineage-driver burden columns might help the tree model separate them better than individual gene splits across the 4,384-column mutation-presence matrix. Target, test distribution, and Public LB do not define or select the gene groups. Single-family ablation against EXP-374.",
